---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";
import "../styles/evidence.css";
import RequestHistory from "../components/app/RequestHistory.astro";
import ClaimHistory from "../components/app/ClaimHistory.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Audit evidence pack · Meridian"
  description="Everything Meridian keeps about one partner funding request: every decision, who made it and when, and the files that were reviewed."
  share="og-evidence-pack.png"
  shareAlt="Meridian: The audit evidence pack. An example record, MDF-000033, closed, with nine files fingerprinted."
>

<main id="main">

<!-- 1 · Hero: words left, the request's summary right -->
<section class="ehero" id="top"><div class="in ehero-grid">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <span class="pill">Sample record</span>
    <h1>The audit<br><em>evidence pack.</em></h1>
    <p class="lead">Everything Meridian keeps about one request: every decision, who made it, and the files reviewed. The data is an example.</p>
    <div class="btns"><a class="btn" href="/request-a-walkthrough">Request a walkthrough</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/controls">See the controls</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="sum card pv">
    <div class="sum-h"><div><b class="mono">MDF-000033</b><small>Brightfold Solutions · Customer summit</small></div><span class="st">Closed</span></div>
    <dl><div><dt>Approved</dt><dd>USD 22,000.00</dd></div><div><dt>Confirmed and invoiced</dt><dd>USD 22,000.00</dd></div><div><dt>Entries in the history</dt><dd>28</dd></div><div><dt>Files, each fingerprinted</dt><dd>9</dd></div></dl>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 2 · The history: one long sheet of glass, with every decision on the line -->
<section class="sec etrail" aria-labelledby="h-trail"><div class="in trail-grid">
  <div class="sheet-wrap">
    <span class="blob eb1"></span><span class="blob eb2"></span>
    <div class="esheet" id="sheet">
      <h2 class="vh" id="h-trail">The history of MDF-000033</h2>
      <span class="eline" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
      <ol class="evs">
        <li class="ev" data-note="3"><div class="ev-h"><h3>Submitted</h3><time datetime="2026-11-03T09:14">3 Nov 2026, 09:14</time></div><p>Jonas Becker · Brightfold Solutions, partner</p><ul class="tags"><li class="tag">Request form v4</li><li class="tag">Approval route v3</li></ul></li>
        <li class="ev" data-note="0"><div class="ev-h"><h3>Approved</h3><time datetime="2026-11-09T09:05">9 Nov 2026, 09:05</time></div><p>Grace Adeyemi · Channels leader · step 3 of 3</p><ul class="tags"><li class="tag">USD 22,000</li><li class="tag ctl"><a href="/controls#c-01">Rule C-01</a></li></ul></li>
        <li class="ev" data-note="2"><div class="ev-h"><h3>Signed and countersigned</h3><time datetime="2026-11-11T09:48">11 Nov 2026, 09:48</time></div><p>Both parties, by secure link</p><ul class="tags"><li class="tag">Countersigned request form</li><li class="tag">faae…dbca</li></ul></li>
        <li class="ev" data-note="1"><div class="ev-h"><h3>Ready</h3><time datetime="2026-11-16T15:20">16 Nov 2026, 15:20</time></div><p>Both signatures, purchase order and campaign reference on file</p><ul class="tags"><li class="tag">PO 6200004812</li><li class="tag ctl"><a href="/controls#c-08">Rule C-08</a></li></ul></li>
        <li class="ev" data-note="2"><div class="ev-h"><h3>Amount confirmed</h3><time datetime="2026-12-08T09:52">8 Dec 2026, 09:52</time></div><p>Samir Haddad · Claims team · 4 files reviewed</p><ul class="tags"><li class="tag">USD 22,000, as approved</li><li class="tag">December 2026 rates</li></ul></li>
        <li class="ev" data-note="1"><div class="ev-h"><h3>Invoice approved and sent to accounts payable</h3><time datetime="2026-12-11T10:24">11 Dec 2026, 10:24</time></div><p>Samir Haddad · Claims team · invoice equals the confirmed amount</p><ul class="tags"><li class="tag">USD 22,000.00</li><li class="tag ctl"><a href="/controls#c-11">Rule C-11</a></li></ul></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
  <aside class="side" aria-label="What you're looking at">
    <p class="side-h">What you're looking at</p>
    <ul class="notes" id="notes">
      <li class="sn"><b>Who, in what role, and when</b><span>On every decision, including corrections.</span></li>
      <li class="sn"><b>The rule behind each step</b><span>Each tag names the control on the Controls page that applies to that step.</span></li>
      <li class="sn"><b>The file that was reviewed</b><span>Fingerprinted on upload, and can't be altered after.</span></li>
      <li class="sn"><b>The rules in force</b><span>The form and route versions it was submitted under.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="side-f">Six of the 28 entries are shown here.</p>
  </aside>
</div></section>

<!-- 2b · The same history in the product: the request's history and its claim's, side by side -->
<section class="sec" id="in-meridian" aria-labelledby="h-same"><div class="in">
  <div class="sec-h rv"><h2 id="h-same">The same history, <em>in Meridian.</em></h2><p class="lead">The request and its claim each keep their own history. This is what your team sees on screen.</p></div>
  <div class="acs req lav">
    <div class="acs-c pv"><span class="pill">On the request</span><RequestHistory /></div>
    <div class="acs-c pv"><span class="pill">On its claim</span><ClaimHistory /></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<!-- 3 · The files: four tinted tiles, then the rules in force -->
<section class="sec" id="files" aria-labelledby="h-files"><div class="in">
  <div class="files-h"><h2 id="h-files" class="rv">Nine files,<br><em>none of them changed.</em></h2><p class="lead rv">Each file is fingerprinted when it's uploaded. Change one character and the fingerprint no longer matches.</p></div>
  <ul class="fgrid">
    <li class="file pv" style="--k:var(--mint)"><i class="doc" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Proof of the event</b><small>3 files: agenda, attendee list, venue photo</small><span class="fp">bc7a…8053 and 2 more</span><span class="st">Accepted</span></li>
    <li class="file pv" style="--k:var(--lav)"><i class="doc" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Invoices</b><small>3 files: the supplier's, and the partner's, sent twice</small><span class="fp">0b1f…ab1c and 2 more</span><span class="st">Approved</span></li>
    <li class="file pv" style="--k:var(--peach)"><i class="doc" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Signed request forms</b><small>2 files: signed, then countersigned</small><span class="fp">8a9e…29ed and faae…dbca</span><span class="st">On file</span></li>
    <li class="file pv" style="--k:var(--sky)"><i class="doc" aria-hidden="true"></i><b>Purchase order</b><small>1 file</small><span class="fp">2cef…d324</span><span class="st">On file</span></li>
  </ul>
  <div class="force rv"><b>In force for this request</b><span class="tag">Request form v4</span><span class="tag">Approval route v3</span><span class="tag">Exchange rates, December 2026</span><a class="lk" href="/controls">See the controls <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
</div></section>

<!-- 4 · Close: one block of solid teal -->
<section class="close" id="walkthrough" aria-labelledby="h-close"><div class="in">
  <div class="blk pv"><h2 id="h-close">See your own process<br>on a record like this.</h2><p>We'll walk one request through with your activity types and your approval rules.</p><a class="btn white" href="/request-a-walkthrough">Request a walkthrough</a></div>
</div></section>

</main>

<script>
  import "../scripts/evidence.js";
</script>
</Base>
